    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 28 Priory Hall is a beautifully presented two-bedroom, third-floor apartment, ideally positioned within this highly sought-after landmarkdevelopment. Tastefully updated and renovated over recent years, the property now comes to the market in excellent condition throughout and offers a stylish, turn-key home in a superb town-centre setting. The well-proportioned accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, two generous double bedrooms, a family bathroom, and a bright, spacious open-plan kitchen, living and dining area. A particular highlight of the apartment is the stunning outlook over the River Slaney, with spectacular views enjoyed from both the main living space and primary bedroom. The property has benefited from a number of recent upgrades, including a new kitchen, upgraded radiators and windows. These improvements have enhanced both the contemporary presentation and overall energy efficiency of the apartment. Externally, the property benefits from a designated parking space to the front of the development.  Wexford town centre is less than 1km away and is easily accessible within walking distance, making this an exceptionally convenient location. The location is truly second to none, with an excellent range of amenities close at hand. Wexford’s vibrant town centre offers a superb selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques, shops and everyday services, all within easy walking distance. Wexford’s Main Street, together with Wexford Train and Bus Station, is approximately 1km from the property, providing excellent connectivity for commuters and visitors alike. No. 28 Priory Hall represents a rare opportunity to acquire a stylish, fully renovated apartment within one of Wexford’s most recognisable and desirable developments. Equally suited to owner-occupiers, relocators and investors, this exceptional property combines modern, low-maintenance living with an enviable town-centre location and wonderful River Slaney views. Not to be missed.  VIEWING HIGHLY RECOMMENDED."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Property Accommodation\r\nHall – (7.2m x 1m),  Timber flooring, wall panelling, Hotpress.\r\nOpen plan Kithcen/Living/Dining room – (6.7m x 5.4m) New Eye & Waist level units & worktop, timber flooring, tiled splashback, custom built cabinetry with storage, feature fireplace, plumbed for appliances, gorgeous\r\nviews over the River Slaney.\r\nBedroom 1- (3.9m x 3.5m), Timber flooring, window seat, views over the River Slaney.\r\nBedroom 2 – (4.3m x 3.5m), Timber flooring, window seat.\r\nBathroom- (2.4m x 2m), WC, WHB, tiled flooring, wall panelling, enclosed rainfall shower.\r\n\r\nOutside: Designated parking space to the front.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, mains sewerage, upgraded electric heaters.\r\nBER: E Ber No: 108827577 Performance indicator: 315.69 Wh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
      },
